Kiyoko, meaning Clean, Pure, Child.

Unlike Kon's earlier works, Tokyo Godfathers is not a story about the thin line between reality and delusion, but rather a twisted sentimental story about family and the value of life.

Our 3 main characters are each running away from their past. The theme of escapism appears again in this film, with alcohol, pets and Kiyoko at the forefront. Ultimately each character represents those left behind by society. Kon tells a powerful story about the intrinsic value of a human being, as each character begins to find their own meaning as they bond with each other.

> A life is a life. Its only born once.

Fantastic film.
